{
  "summary": "This study investigates kinetic-environmental coupling at buried interfaces in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells. Using dual-side in situ photoluminescence, researchers revealed simultaneous nucleation at gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing. Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, exacerbating moisture attack. A self-segregating molecule (NFA) was designed to synchronize crystallization, passivate defects, and form a hydrophobic barrier. This approach achieved 24.84% power conversion efficiency in small cells and 21.46% in mini-modules, maintaining 96.26% efficiency after 1000h damp aging at 85±5% RH.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Simultaneous nucleation occurs at both gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing",
    "Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, exacerbating moisture attack",
    "Self-segregating molecule NFA synchronizes crystallization, passivates defects, and forms a hydrophobic barrier"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes self-segregated interfacial regulation as a rational strategy to overcome kinetic-environmental constraints in scalable flexible perovskite photovoltaics."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the factors influencing early human settlement in the Arabian desert. Using a 1,500-km geoarchaeological survey across Rub' al Khali, researchers found that while freshwater was present, the availability of stone for tool production was a critical independent factor. Palaeolake deposits existed at 55 of 125 sites without lithic artefacts or knappable materials. Spatial modeling indicates settlement required co-occurrence of water and lithic resources, not water alone. This challenges models that prioritize water availability in dispersal predictions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Palaeolake deposits were present at 55 of 125 surveyed sites without lithic artefacts or knappable stone",
    "Spatial modeling shows settlement required co-occurrence of water and lithic resources, not water alone",
    "57% of water-accessible terrain lacks knappable stone, improving site discrimination accuracy to 0.768"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings demonstrate that lithic resource availability, not water alone, constrained early human dispersal patterns across arid regions, refining models of Pleistocene human migration."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated how protein kinase A (PKA) signaling regulates group 3 innate lymphoid cell (ILC3) homeostasis and its role in gut inflammation. Using a single-cell atlas, researchers found that prostaglandin activates PKA to promote tissue-protective functions, while interleukin-23 (IL-23) suppresses PKA inhibitors. Deletion of PRKAR1A reduced ILC3s and increased infection susceptibility in mice, and human ILC3s expressed PRKAR1A, which was downregulated by IL-23 in inflammation. These results indicate PKA signaling is critical for ILC3 maintenance and that IL-23-driven PKA dysregulation causes gut inflammation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "IL-23 suppresses PKA inhibitors in ILC3s, promoting inflammation",
    "PRKAR1A deletion reduced ILC3 numbers and increased enteric infection susceptibility in mice",
    "Human intestinal ILC3s express PRKAR1A, which is downregulated by IL-23 in inflammatory bowel disease"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes PKA signaling as a key regulator of ILC3 homeostasis and demonstrates how IL-23 disrupts this balance to drive gut inflammation, providing mechanistic insights into inflammatory bowel disease pathogenesis."
}

{
  "summary": "This study examines the current state of obesity management medications (OMMs), highlighting advances in understanding obesity pathophysiology that enable rational drug discovery. It identifies key challenges including side effects, variable treatment responses, long-term metabolic changes, and adherence issues that limit existing OMMs. The research suggests developing new medications to address these barriers for sustainable weight loss and improved obesity health outcomes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Advances in understanding obesity pathophysiology enable rational development of obesity management medications",
    "Existing OMMs face limitations due to side effects, heterogeneous treatment responses, and long-term metabolic adaptations",
    "Further medication development is necessary to overcome barriers for sustainable weight loss in obesity management"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This research provides a framework for rationally designing next-generation obesity medications by addressing current limitations in existing therapies, advancing the field toward more effective and sustainable weight management solutions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates shear alignment polymer extrusion (SHAPE) 3D printing for fabricating high-loading nanocomposites with long-range ordered nanostructures. The approach uses high shear forces to align nanofillers like boron nitride nanosheets and carbon nanotubes in polymer matrices, enabling scalable production of complex 3D architectures. Results demonstrate 55 wt% boron nitride in polylactic acid filaments with zero volume shrinkage post-sintering, achieving tailored thermal conductivity (1.07 W/m/K) and mechanical properties for thermal management and structural applications.",
  "key_findings": [
    "SHAPE 3D printing enables high-loading nanocomposites (up to 55 wt% boron nitride) with long-range ordered nanostructures",
    "Post-sintering yields zero volume shrinkage and exceptional thermomechanical stability exceeding polymer melting temperatures",
    "Vertically aligned boron nitride composites exhibit enhanced thermal conductivity (1.07 W/m/K) while horizontally aligned structures provide thermal insulation (0.071 W/m/K)"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a scalable method for cross-scale design of nanocomposites with tailored functionalities, advancing thermal management and structural materials applications through precise nanofiller alignment."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether transient dietary changes during acute inflammation influence long-term tissue immune memory. Using lean mice with type 17 skin inflammation, researchers found that a 4-day high-fat diet (HFD) exposure at disease onset exacerbates inflammation comparably to chronic obesity. The effect is confined to a specific 4-day window; HFD outside this window has no impact. Neutrophils recruited by HFD express NLRP3 and IL-1β, driving pathogenic TH17 cell activation. After recovery on low-fat diet, a chromatin-poised tissue-resident memory T cell population persists, causing exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence. These findings demonstrate that dietary state during a narrow temporal window can durably reprogram disease trajectory through neutrophil-NLRP3-IL-1β mechanisms.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Transient high-fat diet exposure at disease onset exacerbates inflammation in lean mice comparably to chronic obesity",
    "The pro-inflammatory effect is restricted to a 4-day peri-initiation window; HFD outside this window has no impact",
    "Neutrophil-mediated NLRP3-IL-1β signaling licenses pathogenic TH17 cells, with persistent tissue-resident memory T cells after recovery on low-fat diet"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes that short-lived dietary states during acute inflammation can durably reprogram immune memory via neutrophil-NLRP3-IL-1β pathways, revealing a temporal window for dietary interventions to modulate inflammatory disease trajectories."
}

{
  "summary": "This study examines whether current AI systems align with Indigenous scientific principles, emphasizing ethical and environmental safeguards. It argues that present AI configurations risk irreversible harm and thus conflict with Indigenous science's priority of minimizing ecological damage. The research concludes that existing AI lacks ethical and scientific compatibility with Indigenous perspectives, though future AI could potentially align if reconfigured.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Current AI systems pose risks of irreversible environmental harm due to inadequate ethical safeguards",
    "Indigenous science prioritizes minimal ecological damage as a core ethical principle",
    "Present AI configurations are incompatible with Indigenous scientific ethics but future AI may align if reconfigured"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work highlights a critical ethical boundary between current AI development and Indigenous ecological knowledge systems, urging reevaluation of AI design to prevent environmental harm."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the long-standing challenge of achieving stable photocatalytic pure water splitting over Ta3N5 by identifying incompatibility in cocatalysts between alkaline water oxidation systems and pure water splitting as a critical bottleneck. The researchers developed a highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst using a multi-step incipient wetness impregnation strategy. The optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx photocatalyst achieved stoichiometric pure water splitting with an apparent quantum yield of 0.72% at 420 nm, the highest reported for Ta-based nitrides. Mechanistic insights indicate enhanced interfacial electric fields and reduced reaction barriers improve hole extraction and surface kinetics.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx photocatalyst achieved stoichiometric pure water splitting with 0.72% apparent quantum yield at 420 nm, the highest for Ta-based nitrides.",
    "Cocatalyst incompatibility between alkaline water oxidation systems and pure water splitting causes N2 generation via photocorrosion.",
    "Enhanced interfacial electric fields and reduced reaction barriers in the cocatalyst improve hole extraction and surface reaction kinetics."
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes cocatalyst compatibility as a critical design principle for stable photocatalytic pure water splitting and provides mechanistic insights for advancing nitride and oxynitride photocatalysts."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the molecular basis of the female protective effect (FPE) in autism spectrum disorder (ASD). Using human neural progenitor cells, researchers identified transcriptomic convergence among 18 ASD genes, revealing shared downregulation of ASD genes. De novo gene regulatory network reconstruction highlighted CHD8 and REST as central regulators, while X-linked ZFX expression in females was proposed to buffer ASD gene mutations, explaining FPE.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Individual perturbations of 1:8 ASD genes converge on shared downregulation of ASD genes in human neural progenitor cells",
    "Central transcriptional regulators CHD8 and REST drive transcriptomic convergence among ASD genes",
    "X-linked ZFX expression in females buffers ASD gene mutations, contributing to the female protective effect"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides molecular mechanisms underlying the female protective effect in autism by identifying convergent gene regulatory networks and X-linked factors that mitigate ASD risk in females."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated how dietary fiber impacts androgen levels in polyendocrine metabolic ovarian syndrome (PMOS). Using a clinical trial with inulin, resistant starch, and β-glucan, researchers observed reduced plasma androgens. Mechanistically, dietary fiber increased Bacteroides xylanisolvens, which converts androstenedione to coproandrosterone—a nonandrogenic metabolite—further processed into dihydro-coproandroone. The pathway was confirmed in mice, suggesting dietary fiber modulates androgen homeostasis via gut microbiota to alleviate PMOS.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Dietary fiber combinations reduced plasma androgen concentrations in PMOS patients",
    "Bacteroides xylanisolvens increased and converted androstenedione to coproandrosterone",
    "The coproandrosterone pathway was validated in mouse models"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a gut microbiota-mediated mechanism by which dietary fiber regulates androgen metabolism, providing a foundation for targeted interventions in PMOS."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how heterointerfacial bonding affects service stability in flexible perovskite photovoltaics. By blending polyamide curing agents with fullerene derivatives, researchers created a multi-bond network that enhances covalent anchoring and hydrogen bonding for improved energy dissipation. The resulting 100 cm² module achieved 22.33% power conversion efficiency (certified 2.15%) and maintained performance after 5,000 bending cycles under UV irradiation, demonstrating exceptional stability against multi-stress coupling.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A polyamide-cured fullerene blend forms a multi-bond network with covalent and hydrogen bonding for enhanced interfacial stability",
    "The 100 cm² perovskite solar module achieved 22.33% certified power conversion efficiency",
    "The module retained performance after 5,000 consecutive bending cycles under UV irradiation without significant degradation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a novel heterointerfacial bonding strategy that enables flexible perovskite photovoltaics to maintain stability under multi-stress conditions, advancing the field of durable organic photovoltaic devices."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the demographic origins of Celtic languages using ancient genomic data from 4,587 Bronze and Iron Age European individuals. By analyzing genome-wide data, it identifies three key population movements: Steppe-related ancestry arriving via Bell Beaker groups around 4400 BP, a Bronze Age migration from southwestern Europe to Britain, and a westward expansion of eastern central European ancestry (3200-2800 BP) affecting France, the British Isles, Iberia, and Italy. The findings suggest the eastern central European migration is most parsimonious for Celtic spread, though language shifts may not directly track genetic changes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Steppe-related ancestry entered Europe via Bell Beaker groups approximately 4400 years ago",
    "Bronze Age migration from southwestern Europe to Britain occurred between 3800-3200 BP",
    "Eastern central European ancestry expanded westward from 3200-2800 BP, influencing regions where Celtic languages later emerged"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides genomic evidence for the demographic processes that most plausibly facilitated the spread of Celtic languages across prehistoric Europe, clarifying the genetic pathways associated with their historical distribution."
}

{
  "summary": "This study developed FIND, a high-throughput method using DNA nanoswitches and next-generation sequencing to identify molecular modulators of protein-protein interactions. It discovered nanobodies stabilizing ACE2-SARS-CoV-2 receptor binding and agonists for peroxisome proliferator-using receptor gamma. The approach enables rapid therapeutic discovery for conditions involving protein interactions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "FIND identified nanobodies that stabilize ACE2-SARS-CoV-2 receptor binding",
    "FIND discovered agonists for peroxisome proliferator-activated receptor gamma",
    "The method enables ultrahigh-throughput screening of protein-protein interaction modulators"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This approach provides a scalable platform for discovering therapeutic modulators of protein-protein interactions, accelerating the development of treatments for diseases involving such interactions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates threo-chiral cation additives for enhancing perovskite solar cell stability and efficiency. Using (2S,3R)-2-amino-3-hydroxybutanamide hydrochloride (ThrA), researchers achieved precise lattice regulation via stereoselective hydrogen bonding and lead coordination. The approach reduced surface energy, promoted (100) crystal growth, and suppressed defects. ThrA-modified cells reached 26.68% certified efficiency and maintained 90% performance after 1000h thermal aging.",
  "key_findings": [
    "ThrA's threo-configuration enables conformationally locked rigid stereostructure for stereoselective adsorption",
    "ThrA-modified cells achieved 26.68% certified efficiency and 22.78% for 65 cm² modules",
    "Unencapsulated devices retained 90% initial efficiency after 1000h thermal aging"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes stereochemical control as a critical factor for optimizing perovskite crystallization, advancing strategies for high-efficiency and ultra-stable photovoltaic devices."
}

{
  "summary": "This study performed a phenome-wide association study (PheWAS) analyzing 12.8 million gut microbial single-nucleotide variants (SNVs) across 244 health phenotypes and exposures in 10,781 individuals. It identified 940 independent associations linking microbial SNVs to host factors like age, sex, and metabolic parameters. Structural analyses revealed SNVs in functionally critical protein regions, suggesting mechanisms by which microbial genetic variation influences host health and environmental interactions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "940 independent associations between gut microbial SNVs and 69 host factors including age, sex, and cardiovascular/metabolic parameters",
    "Identification of age-associated SNVs in Faecalibacterium prausnitzii affecting glutathione-binding protein regions",
    "Structural insights into how microbial genetic variants impact host health through protein functional regions"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes base-pair resolution links between gut microbial genetic variation and host health phenotypes, providing a resource for mechanistic hypotheses about strain-level microbiome functionality."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the timescale of Atlantic Meridional Overturning Circulation (AMOC) changes during Dansgaard-Oeschger (DO) events using speleothem oxygen-isotope records. The research demonstrates that AMOC recovery took over a century, contrasting with Greenland ice cores indicating warming within decades. The findings reveal that initial atmospheric reorganization preceded slower oceanic adjustments, challenging the perception of abrupt AMOC transitions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "AMOC recovery during DO events spanned over a century, not decades as ice cores suggest",
    "Greenland ice cores capture rapid atmospheric reorganization from initial sea-ice retreat",
    "Oceanic thermal adjustment occurred significantly slower than atmospheric changes"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study clarifies that natural AMOC transitions are more gradual than Greenland ice core records imply, refining the understanding of abrupt climate shifts during past ice ages."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing slot-die coating for perovskite solar cells by expanding the processing window. Using rubidium and formamidinium thiocyanates as additives, the researchers broadened the deposition-to-annealing time window beyond 100 seconds. This approach achieved uniform crystallization, minimized compositional gradients, and improved device efficiency to 22.70% with stable performance over 1300 hours under ambient conditions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Broadened processing window exceeding 100 seconds for slot-die coating",
    "Uniform crystallization with minimized vertical compositional gradients",
    "22.10% efficiency with 97.76% retention after 1300 hours under ISOS-L-3"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a generalizable method for decoupling crystallization kinetics from processing constraints in scalable perovskite photovoltaic fabrication."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated how endothelial cells (ECs) adapt to the absence of VEGFR2 signaling during angiogenesis. Using genetic mosaics, researchers found that Vegfr2KO ECs initially fail to sprout but later dominate venous networks, enabling VEGF-independent angiogenesis. Molecular analysis revealed compensatory mechanisms involving VEGFR1 and V. The findings highlight venousization as a key adaptation strategy to VEGF signaling loss.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Vegfr2KO endothelial cells initially fail sprouting but become dominant in veins",
    "VEGFR1 partially compensates for VEGFR2 loss in capillary cells, while VEGFR3 compensates in arterial cells",
    "Loss of NR2F2 significantly impairs expansion of Vegfr2KO endothelial cells"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study demonstrates venousization as a critical mechanism for endothelial adaptation and resistance to VEGF signaling loss during angiogenesis, providing insights into vascular development and therapeutic resistance."
}

{
  "summary": "This study developed BlueDown, a postprocessing algorithm for US Census data using differential privacy. It combines regression and constrained optimization to reduce error in county-level racial groupings by 21-36% and all county-level groupings by 9-58%. At the tract level, it improved housing type groupings by 38-61%. The approach enhances data validity without compromising confidentiality or computational efficiency, supporting federal spending decisions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "BlueDown reduced county-level racial grouping errors by 21-36%",
    "All county-level grouping errors decreased by 9-58%",
    "Tract-level housing type grouping errors were reduced by 38-61%"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work advances differential privacy by providing a highly efficient postprocessing method that significantly improves data accuracy while maintaining confidentiality, directly benefiting large-scale demographic analyses and policy decisions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated ROS-driven GSDMD palmitoylation in sepsis using PBMCs from patients. Researchers identified ZDHHC5/ZDHHC9 transferases as key mediators and developed vanadium oxide hydroxide nanosheets (VOOH NSs) to scavenge ROS and inhibit palmitoylation. The intervention reduced pyroptosis, inflammation, and sepsis severity in animal models, with validation in GSDMD-knockout mice confirming the pathway's therapeutic relevance.",
  "key_findings": [
    "GSDMD palmitoylation in septic PBMCs is enhanced by ROS via ZDHHC5/ZDHHC9 transferases",
    "VOOH NSs inhibit ROS and palmitoylation, reducing pyroptosis and inflammation",
    "GSDMD-knockout mice validation confirms palmitoylation pathway as a therapeutic target"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "Targeting ROS-mediated GSDMD palmitoylation provides a novel mechanism to mitigate sepsis progression by inhibiting pyroptosis and inflammatory damage."
}

{
  "summary": "This study identifies nectin-4 as a functional receptor for rubella virus (RuV) entry in airway and placental cells. Using proximity biotin labelling proteomics and CRISPR-Cas9 validation, researchers demonstrated that nectin-4 mediates RuV attachment, endocytosis, and infection in both cell types. The findings reveal nectin-4's role in respiratory transmission and early placental infection, with implications for therapeutic targeting.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Nectin-4 directly interacts with RuV envelope glycoproteins to facilitate entry",
    "Nectin-4 enables basolateral RuV entry in airway epithelia and apical progeny release",
    "Nectin-4 is highly expressed on placental syncytiotrophoblasts, supporting maternal-fetal interface infection"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes nectin-4 as a critical receptor for rubella virus transmission across respiratory and placental barriers, providing a molecular basis for understanding congenital rubella syndrome pathogenesis and potential therapeutic interventions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the origin of the pseudogap in cuprate high-temperature superconductors using local shot-noise spectroscopy on Bi2Sr2CaCu2O8+δ. The research demonstrates that the pseudogap energy aligns with electron pairing onset and exhibits spatial heterogeneity up to 70 meV. The findings support a pairing mechanism over local order, indicating phase coherence limits critical temperature in cuprates.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The pseudogap energy coincides with electron pairing onset",
    "The pseudogap exhibits spatial heterogeneity with values up to 70 milli-electron volts",
    "The results exclude a pure local order origin for the pseudogap"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides direct evidence linking pseudogap formation to Cooper pair dynamics in cuprates, advancing understanding of the interplay between superconductivity and pseudogap phenomena."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates photothermal catalytic dry reforming of methane using a Rh/Mg2V1.33O4 catalyst with defective spinel vanadate. The catalyst leverages interfacial redox shuttling between Rh and vanadate species to enable lattice oxygen migration, achieving 1000-hour stability and high syng. The approach enhances coking resistance and light-to-chemical energy efficiency to ∼20.9% under solar irradiation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "1000-hour operational stability in photothermal methane dry reforming",
    "Interfacial redox shuttle mechanism enabling lattice oxygen migration",
    "High syngas production rates (16.1 mol gRh-1 h-1 H2, 18.6 mol gRh-1 h-1 CO) and 20.9% light-to-chemical energy efficiency"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes quasi-metallic vanadate supports as a durable platform for lattice oxygen-mediated photothermal catalysis, advancing stability and efficiency in greenhouse gas conversion."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated glioblastoma heterogeneity by generating a deep single-cell and spatial multi-omic atlas of 12 human tumours. It identified a spatiotemporal cancer cell trajectory where cells transition from developmental-like states to glial injury response and hypoxia-defined states. This trajectory regionalizes tumours into distinct microenvironments, shows molecular conservation across tumours, and links to myeloid heterogeneity through spatially intermixed subclones.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Glioblastoma heterogeneity arises from spatially patterned transitions of cancer cells from developmental-like states to glial injury response and hypoxia-defined states",
    "The cellular trajectory regionalizes tumours into distinct tissue microenvironments with molecular conservation across tumours",
    "Tumour subclones are spatially intermixed through microenvironments and linked to myeloid heterogeneity"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a stereotyped spatiotemporal trajectory of cancer cells in glioblastoma, providing a unified framework for understanding tumour heterogeneity through cellular and tissue dynamics."
}
